sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 7 of the command pipeline (feature-flow section 7). After each release and at least daily, every task VM host refreshes its own task image and topology seed, in parallel; ready slots built from the old image are replaced one at a time. Nothing is copied between hosts.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: pipeline stage 7 · per-host task image and seed refresh
  %% kind: pipeline.7-task-image-seed-refresh
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=each host tone=amber
  %% lane SL icon=server pill=pool tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>one run per host
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant SL as Ready slots<br/>stopped task VMs
  Note over GW: Start the refresh<br/>after a release · daily
  %%> Triggers:
  %%> - a release that went live and passed its check (stage 6)
  %%> - a daily schedule, so a seed never gets older than a day: the Swamp tokens in the ready copies last 24 hours and a ready copy expires after 20
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - both triggers (B8); today an operator runs `php artisan task-vms:refresh-seed HOST`
  %%> Requirements per host:
  %%> - an active task VM host with no image build running and three free large slots
  %%> - the Gateway has the release commit, GitHub App read access to the repository, and the proof Swamp Club key
  GW->>SW: Start one run per host<br/>all in parallel
  %%> Why:
  %%> - hosts differ in CPU, and a copy between hosts loses the storage sharing inside the seed; so each host builds its own
  %%> - a second admission for a host returns the open task
  loop each task VM host, in parallel
    SW->>H: Build the task image<br/>from the recipe
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - builds a builder VM from the stock image, runs the recipe phases, smoke-tests it and publishes it
    %%> - promotes the image only when built and smoke-tested; a failed build leaves the previous image
    %%> Chart:
    %%> - `task_vm.image_build`
    %%> Target, not built:
    %%> - the build uses the same playbooks as Nodes and no orbit-agent
    SW->>H: Refresh the topology seed<br/>release commit
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - clones the current seed, boots a builder from the new image, checks out the release commit, runs `proof-fleet reset` and `ready`
    %%> - boots a throwaway copy of each ready copy to check it, stops the builder, and promotes the clone under the host lock
    %%> - keeps the old seed as `-previous`, the rollback copy; cleanup always runs
    %%> Chart:
    %%> - `task_vm.seed_refresh`
    SW->>SL: Replace old ready slots<br/>one at a time
    %%> Target, not built:
    %%> - destroys a ready slot made from the old image, enrols a new one from the new image, then takes the next
    %%> - a slot is always ready; a slot in use keeps running on its own clone
    %%> - when the image did not change, nothing is replaced
  end
  alt every host refreshed
    SW-->>GW: Host refreshed<br/>terminal event per host
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - each host reports its own result; one slow host does not hold the others
    Note over GW: Record the new seed<br/>claims use it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the next task VM and the next proof start from the new seed, which holds the running release
    %%> - no fleet test follows; the seed is checked only by its own throwaway boot
  else a build or refresh failed
    SW--xGW: Host not refreshed<br/>previous seed stays
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the failed step is named; the host keeps the image and seed it had, and the next trigger tries again
    Note over GW: Alert · try again<br/>next trigger
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the host keeps the image and seed it had; the other hosts are not affected
  end
